    {
      "id": "claim_06f077d771784429bd91fad8eaf7a5f6",
      "statement": "models/__init__.py imports some models purely so they are always registered with the Django app registry, because processes that skipped feature code otherwise did not know their tables existed and the test-database TRUNCATE flush failed on their foreign keys. MapLayer is deliberately not imported, since it has no migration and importing it breaks test-database creation.",
